{
 "method_card": {
  "steps": [
   "CF: add running totals and plot at upper boundaries",
   "Read Q1, median, Q3 from the CF curve",
   "Box plots: draw using the 5-number summary",
   "Histograms: frequency = FD × class width"
  ],
  "title": "Cumulative Frequency, Box Plots & Histograms",
  "content": "<p><strong>Cumulative frequency (CF):</strong> Running total of frequencies. Plot at <strong>upper class boundaries</strong> and join with a smooth curve. Read off: <strong>median</strong> at \\(n/2\\), <strong>Q1</strong> at \\(n/4\\), <strong>Q3</strong> at \\(3n/4\\). <strong>IQR</strong> = Q3 − Q1.</p><p><strong>Box plots:</strong> Show min, Q1, median, Q3, max. The box spans the IQR. Useful for comparing distributions.</p><p><strong>Histograms:</strong> Use <strong>frequency density</strong> on the y-axis. FD = frequency ÷ class width. The <strong>area</strong> of each bar = frequency. Unequal class widths are standard.</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>CF of 60 values: Q1 at 15th = 22, Median at 30th = 35, Q3 at 45th = 48.</strong></p><p>IQR = 48 − 22 = 26.</p>"
 },
